Solace/Reverie: Quest into the Dreamscape (developed as DreamQuest)
Copyright (c) 2026 Dexsidius

The game is two kinds of work under two licences: its code under the MIT
License, and the game itself -- its art, music, maps, story and writing --
under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0.


THE GAME'S CONTENT -- CC BY-NC-SA 4.0

These are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-
ShareAlike 4.0 International licence,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/ :

- The art: every image under assets/ and art/, and the tools in tools/ that
  model, draw, paint, cut or render it (the blender_*.py scripts, the make_*
  scripts, character_palettes.py, tilecut.cpp and icons.txt).
- The music and sound effects, as composed in src/systems/audio.cpp.
- The maps under maps/, and the places tools/genmaps.cpp lays out.
- The story, quests, dialogue, items and every other piece of writing under
  data/, and tools/make_story.py, which writes the story's.

In short: you may share it and make things from it, as long as you credit
Dexsidius and link the licence, never for money, and share what you make
under the same licence. Selling it, or anything made from it, needs written
permission from Dexsidius. The licence's own text is what counts; that
summary is not a substitute for it.

Where one file holds both kinds of work -- audio.cpp's synthesiser is code,
its tunes are content -- each part keeps its own licence.


